  "summary": "Seven preprints show agent performance in biology depends on scaffolding, grounding and benchmarks, with new tools for evidence synthesis and foundation-model…",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that reliability of LLM agents in biology is being set by infrastructure around the model rather than by the model alone. ABCD-Stack attributes hypothesis quality to the prompting harness, not model tier, and DTDR scaffolding raises a bioinformatics sandbox agent from 0% to 9.09% accuracy while cutting steps 66%. GLESKit and LabWeaver ground outputs in retained workspaces, gene-level resources, literature and laboratory-tier memory and skills. BioResearchBench (50 expert-written tasks) and AutoSPECTRA, a coding-agent audit of foundation-model generalizability, add evaluation, while AI-FAIR metadata criteria address dataset readiness. New relative to earlier work is the pairing of agents with reviewable evidence trails and systematic audit protocols. The previous synthesis's EDB-Bio and PPI-Caliper are not supported by the current items.",
